        "original_id": "2aca4459-47be-5c80-8e78-df47359e16da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hilda Neihardt, John G. Neihardt, Black Elk\n- Works: Black Elk Speaks\n- Roles: official observer, Oglala Lakota medicine man, Lakota holy man\n\nFacts:\n- In 1932, John G. Neihardt published Black Elk Speaks, a book that relates the story of Black Elk, an Oglala Lakota medicine man.\n- At age 15, Hilda Neihardt accompanied her father John G. Neihardt as an official observer to meetings with Black Elk.\n- Hilda Neihardt was born in 1916 and died in 2004.\n- John G. Neihardt described Hilda Neihardt as one of his comrades in adventure.\n- The life stories of Black Elk formed the basis for John G. Neihardt's book Black Elk Speaks and for Hilda Neihardt's later works.",
